.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The payload is always NUL\-terminated for convenience, but
\f[CR]*payload_len\f[R] gives the actual byte count.
.IP \(bu 2
For binary framing, unknown channels (> \f[CR]CHAN_MAX\f[R]) cause the
payload to be read and discarded before returning \-1.
.IP \(bu 2
For NDJSON framing, the buffer grows dynamically (starting at 1024
bytes, doubling as needed) up to \f[CR]FRAME_MAX_PAYLOAD + 64\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]EINTR\f[R] during \f[CR]read(2)\f[R] is handled internally in both
formats.
.IP \(bu 2
The function reads exactly the number of bytes specified by the header
(binary) or until newline (NDJSON).
It does not over\-read.
